{"attachment": {"content": "- worldlabs:atlas-blender: Use Blender to see and shape Atlas scenes in 3D. Load posed images as cameras and point clouds, place cameras by eye, animate a camera path, view splats, and optionally run Atlas tasks from inside Blender with the Atlas add-on. Use when Blender is installed or the user works in Blender.\n- worldlabs:atlas-flythrough: Make a camera-move video through a scene (flythrough, walkthrough, orbit, push-in, pan) from one or more photos or a generated image with World Labs Atlas. Use when the user wants a video or a camera move from images, or new angles of a scene that may become one.\n- worldlabs:atlas-splats: Turn one or more photos or a generated image into a 3D scene as Gaussian splats (an SPZ file) with World Labs Atlas. Use when the user wants a 3D scene, a world to explore, splats, or a scene to view, export or mesh from images, or new angles and views of a place from an image.\n- worldlabs:worldlabs-cli: Run World Labs Atlas API tasks from a terminal with the worldlabs CLI. Covers install and sign-in, uploading files, running a task from a JSON request, waiting for it, and downloading its outputs. Use for any Atlas job without a skill of its own, such as generating or editing an image, estimating camera and depth, or extracting a mesh, and for CLI setup and errors. New views of a scene belong to atlas-splats or atlas-flythrough. Also covers the connected World Labs tools when there is no shell.", "digests": ["7b1e2f528d0f93b0", "60ac7cd1d57d57ba", "d0638fbbb6ac059d", "6159a336d356a076"], "isInitial": false, "names": ["worldlabs:atlas-blender", "worldlabs:atlas-flythrough", "worldlabs:atlas-splats", "worldlabs:worldlabs-cli"], "skillCount": 4, "type": "skill_listing"}, "cwd": "/home/user/rainbow-", "entrypoint": "remote_mobile", "gitBranch": "ccr-b0757dec-dj6l1o", "isSidechain": false, "parentUuid": "fbfc6086-5b59-46b0-9475-42a8b64100f8", "rendered": [{"content": "<system-reminder>\nThe following skills are availa